          "Prompt: \"How should I name your sections and agent groups?\" - \"Use clear defaults\" - \"Call parallel groups Armies\" - \"Call them Squads\" - \"Call them Crews\" - \"Call them Pods\" - \"Match my existing company language\" - \"Let me name everything\" If personalized, ask only for the labels they want to change: Strategy section, Research section, Execution/Outbound section, Operations section, one temporary worker, and a parallel worker group. Save a semantic-to-display label map.",
          "Examples are Leaders, HQ, Research, Intel, Army, Squad, Crew, Pod, Outbound, Launch, and Ops. Never force these examples. HARD RULES Use sourced facts or mark Unknown. Respect scope, ownership, suppression, and permissions. External messages and system changes remain drafts until the exact action is confirmed. Work standalone; siblings are optional."
