        "text": "Eng principle: keep PRs scoped. If a bug fix balloons into a churny hardening effort in an adjacent subsystem, SPLIT it — ship the small real fix now, spin the hardening into its OWN follow-up PR designed cleanly from the ground up. Don't let one PR accumulate rounds of edge-case patches.",
